{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 41,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Keep silence before me, O isles; and let the people renew ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strength: let them come near; then let them speak: let us come near together to judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who raised up the righteous ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the east, called him to his foot, gave the nations before him, and made ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rule over kings? he gave ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as the dust to his sword, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as driven stubble to his bow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He pursued them, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " passed safely; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by the way ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he had not gone with his feet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath wrought and done ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", calling the generations from the beginning? I the LORD, the first, and with the last; I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The isles saw ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and feared; the ends of the earth were afraid, drew near, and came.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They helped every one his neighbor; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "every one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " said to his brother, Be of good courage.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So the carpenter encouraged the goldsmith, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that smootheth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the hammer him that smote the anvil, saying, It ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ready for the sodering: and he fastened it with nails, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it should not be moved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But thou, Israel, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my servant, Jacob whom I have chosen, the seed of Abraham my friend.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " whom I have taken from the ends of the earth, and called thee from the chief men thereof, and said to thee, Thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my servant; I have chosen thee, and not cast thee away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fear thou not; for I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thee: be not dismayed; for I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy God: I will strengthen thee; yes, I will help thee; yes, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they that were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " incensed against thee shall be ashamed and confounded: they shall be as nothing; and they that contend with thee shall perish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt seek them, and shalt not find them, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " them that contended with thee: they that war against thee shall be as nothing, and as a thing of naught.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I the LORD thy God will hold thy right hand, saying to thee, Fear not; I will help thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fear not, thou worm Jacob, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye men of Israel; I will help thee, saith the LORD, and thy Redeemer, the Holy One of Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I will make thee a new sharp threshing instrument having teeth: thou shalt thresh the mountains, and beat ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " small, and shalt make the hills as chaff.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt fan them, and the wind shall carry them away, and the whirlwind shall scatter them: and thou shalt rejoice in the LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shalt glory in the Holy One of Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the poor and needy seek water, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their tongue faileth for thirst, I the LORD will hear them, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "I",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the God of Israel will not forsake them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will open rivers in high places, and fountains in the midst of the valleys: I will make the wilderness a pool of water, and the dry land springs of water.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will plant in the wilderness the cedar, the shittah-tree, and the myrtle, and the oil-tree; I will set in the desert the fir-tree, the pine, and the box-tree together:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That they may see, and know, and consider, and understand together, that the hand of the LORD hath done this, and the Holy One of Israel hath created it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Produce your cause, saith the LORD; bring forth your strong ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "reasons",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", saith the King of Jacob.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them bring ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " forth, and show us what shall happen: let them show the former things, what they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that we may consider them, and know the latter end of them; or declare to us things to come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Show the things that are to come hereafter, that we may know that ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " gods: yes, do good, or do evil, that we may be dismayed, and behold ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of nothing, and your work of naught: an abomination ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is he that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " chooseth you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have raised up ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the north, and he shall come: from the rising of the sun shall he call upon my name: and he shall come upon princes as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "upon",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mortar, and as the potter treadeth clay.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath declared from the beginning, that we may know? and before time, that we may say, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "He is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " righteous? verily, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none that showeth, verily, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none that declareth, verily, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none that heareth your words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The first ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall say",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Zion, Behold, behold them: and I will give to Jerusalem one that bringeth good tidings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I beheld, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no man; even among them, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no counselor, that, when I asked of them, could answer a word.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.41.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.41.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all vanity, their works ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " nothing: their molten images ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wind and confusion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
